---
// Site-wide "factual information, not financial advice" notice.
//
// Term deposits are financial advice products under the FMC Act (a debt security
// per s 8(1)(a) -> financial product per s 7(1)(a)), so ranking them is only safe
// while the site stays inside the Schedule 5 cl 7(a) exclusion: providing factual
// information. Every rates page therefore states, in its own words, that it sorts
// published rates by number rather than recommending a product to a reader.
//
// Wording deliberately mirrors the longer notices already inline on index.astro,
// pie-term-deposit-rates.astro and term-deposit-rates-for-seniors.astro — those
// predate this component and are left in place.
interface Props {
  /** Extra classes on the wrapper, e.g. spacing for a page that isn't in a section. */
  class?: string;
}
const { class: className = "" } = Astro.props;
---
<div class={`max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 ${className}`}>
  <div class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6">
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">
      <strong>Not financial advice:</strong> this page provides factual information only. It lists
      publicly published term deposit rates ranked by interest rate, and does not take into account
      your financial situation, goals or risk tolerance. Rates are collected once a day and may not
      match a bank's current offer — confirm the rate, minimum deposit,
      fees and break conditions directly with the bank before investing. Deposits with a licensed
      deposit taker are covered by the Depositor Compensation Scheme up to $100,000 per depositor,
      per institution; amounts above that are not. For advice about your own circumstances, speak to
      a licensed financial advice provider.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
